From ccded1c3ea325186de92ed37dec0969324a78d38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the end of native output is never kept waiting
 by a setting that the driver will not take back; the signals always go

The commit that gives the output back carried every property that the
transport sets, and a refusal of it was tested with all of them as one
base that is never left out: the signals of the transport and the colour
policy alike. A setting that the mode of that commit cannot carry kept it
refused for good. amdgpu (Linux 7.3) refuses a "color format" that the
stream of the mode cannot have (dm_validate_stream_color_format():
YCbCr 4:2:0 in a mode that the display does not list for it), and the
format found is the one of the mode of the video: with "Colour format"
set to YCbCr 4:2:0, a video in a mode that the display takes in 4:2:0, and
the end joined to the change to a mode of the menus that it does not take
in 4:2:0, the tests of the plan (in the mode on the output) were taken and
the commit refused, again each second, for ever. The TV stayed in the mode
of the transport and the menus were not seen. The same where native output
moved to another mode during the video (CDVModeMove): there the base itself
was refused, and taken for a display that refuses everything. HDR metadata
of a video found at the start, which the end puts back, is refused the
same way by a display that does not declare its EOTF.

What the transport sets is now of two kinds (OUTPUT_STATE::PartOf()):

- its signals (DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB and the Low-Latency, HDMI 1.4b and
  HDR tunnel flags of the kernel; NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA and the signalling
  that goes with it on nvidia-drm), which tell the display that the
  transport is on. They are the base: every attempt carries them, and a
  refusal of them alone is still the display refusing, asked again as it
  is. A property that the table does not name is a signal.
- the settings that it makes neutral (the depth, the range, the
  colorimetry, the colour format, the HDR metadata, the dithering, HDMI
  VRR, the colour processing of the CRTC and the plane), none of them
  Dolby Vision: a choice of the user or a state of Kodi. Each is tested on
  top of the signals; one that the driver will not take back stays at the
  transport's value for the rest of the capture (with which the menus show
  as they are), the log says it with the error of the driver, and Kodi
  asks for its own again with its next change of mode (StageOutputFormat()
  puts the user's colour format back there, with its own fallback where
  that mode does not take it either).

Where the commit keeps being refused while its plan is taken in the tests
(what is refused is not in them: the change of mode that goes with it), the
settings that depend on the mode or the display (the colour format and the
HDR metadata) stay at the transport's value after the second refusal, and
every setting after the fifth, when, as before, what the transport did not
set is left as it is: only the signals are asked then. The settings of Kodi
said for the end are not asked again for one that stays so. The plan of
the end and the read back say these apart, and so does the last line of
the end.

The host test of the output state expresses the rule: its check that the
colour format refused was never left out (6d) is now that a preference of
the user that the mode does not take falls to the transport's AUTO, with
the signals never left out (a refused signal still keeps every attempt the
same); its check of commits refused while the tests are taken (6b) follows
the two steps. New: amdgpu with YCbCr 4:2:0 found and the end joined to a
mode that does not take it (given back with the third attempt, the rest as
found), the same after a move into such a mode (the second attempt), and
every setting of a kernel driver and of nvidia-drm refused alone (it stays
at the transport's value, the signal goes). 610 checks; three mutants (the
table that makes everything a signal, no first step for the settings of
the mode, a setting refused in the tests dropped as before) fail it.
